<title>JAPAN: Citizen Watch up on share repurchase plan.</title>
<headline>Citizen Watch up on share repurchase plan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Citizen Watch Co Ltd rose on Tuesday morning on the Tokyo Stock Exchange due to the company's share repurchase plan, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0120 GMT, Citizen Watch's shares were up 39 yen at 967 yen.</p>
<p>Its turnover was 187,000 shares.  </p>
<p>The Japanese watchmaker said on Monday that its board members had approved the share repurchase plan, under which the company would buy back 12 million shares, or 10 billion yen worth of shares.</p>
<p>The company added that it would actually buy 10.66 million shares at 938 yen per share between Tuesday and September 8.</p>
